hello my name is dr brady carter and i'm  a senior application scientist with new  tech group  and i want to thank you for your  interest in my poster titled the role of  water activity in cannabis quality and  safety  the purpose of this poster was to  provide additional information about  why water activity is important  is an important measurement in the  cannabis industry  and you'll notice that water activity is  now starting to show up on most  state regulations as a required test  and the reason is is because water  activity is related to  many different stability factors in  cannabis  as well as in all types of other  products and water activity has been  used for many  years in the food industry effectively  as a  critical control point it also has that  level of importance in cannabis  so water activity is the energy of water  in a product it is not the free water  it's not the available water  although those terms are used often it  is actually the  energy of the water as derived from  fundamentals of thermodynamics  and so it's important to understand that  distinction because the reason why water  activity does what it does is because  it is showing the energy and one of the  main things that water tv is known for  is its ability to be able to control  microbial growth  and that's one of the main roles it  plays within cannabis  because if you get below a water  activity of 0.7  you've essentially shut down the growth  of all types of  microorganisms there are some molds that  will grow below that but they're not  very common spoilage  molds so if you can get it down below  0.7  then you can and store it that way the  dried cannabis flower won't be  susceptible to mold growth and of course  mold  growth in particularly in cannabis can  be  can be quite dangerous both from  mycotoxin production standpoint but also  because mold spores present  and are inhaled can lead to asthma  but water activity isn't just related to  microbial spoilage as you'll see in  table 1  it's also related to many other  stability factors including chemical  stability  physical stability it affects texture  it affects performance and in particular  in cannabis  as the water activity gets too low the  trichomes on the cannabis as shown in  figure two  start to stiffen and to dry out and they  allow  the evaporation or the evaporating off  of the terpenes and the cannabinoids  and so it it actually is detrimental to  over dry cannabis flowers to to drive a  water activity  and so the ideal water activity range  for cannabis as identified in the astm  standard is  to have a water activity between 0.55  and 0.65  and the reason why this is considered to  be ideal is because  in that range you stop mold growth but  you minimize  the amount of trichome destruction um  and you minimize then the evaporation or  loss of  terpenes and cannabinoids and there  really is no advantage in over drying  there's actually disadvantages  uh to being to being uh or to doing that  and it's important to understand that  that's not driven by moisture content  it's driven by water activity so figure  one shows uh  the moisture absorption isotherm for  cannabis  and there's two curves on here there's  an adsorption curve and a desorption  curve and they are not the same because  of hysteresis  and if we target a 0.62 water activity  the moisture content will be different  if we dry to that point than if you wet  to that point so there's no advantage in  over drying  and trying to wet back up to that water  activity because your moisture content  will actually be less  and you want to maximize that amount of  moisture for  many different reasons and so  moisture content isn't what should be  triggering that decision  it should be based your dry down all  should be controlled through water  activity  trying to target that critical range of  0.55 to 0.65  and in so doing you maximize your  profitability by maximizing your weight  from water you're not over drying you're  not using more energy  so all that comes down to water activity  really playing a critical role  in terms of cannabis quality and safety  and it really needs to be a test that's  run  not only just by testing labs to meet  regulations but it should be utilized by  cultivators and processors to make sure  that they're  getting the they're drying that cannabis  flower to the correct  uh water activity so that it will store  and have its maximum shelf  life as well as not posing any kind of  threat to anyone who consumes it  thank you very much for your attention  uh if you have any questions please feel  free to  reach out and contact me uh at  b carter at newtekgroup.com  or visit our website at www  thank you
 

